**Declared actions.** This step MUST do exactly these, and the worker base prompt says what each verb obliges:
- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SlotBarTests`

**How to implement.** The slot bar above the table, in a file of its own (001 §J 'Quick swap: a slot bar above the table shows one chip per slot (`Source: Laser | Prep: CPL1 ▾ | Obj 1: QZ ▾ @ 45° ▾ | … | Detector: Phone`); each dropdown lists compatible items only; choosing one is either a new setup or an existing one; keyboard: Tab between chips, letters pick'; 001 §O 'Slot bar over the table (§J), with "Record experiment"' and 'Automation': `SlotChip_<slot>`; the S8.4 brief; .spec-md §4 'UI'). The bar sits inside the main page directly above the table, so it is compiled before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs` as a projection of its own state and handler records, the shape of the Experiments bay (`ExperimentControls.fs:experimentControlsView`, over the handlers `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:experimentHandlers` builds), and the main view docks it. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.4. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: a new group after the flow-strip group (step 242), `// --- The slot bar over the table (SlotBarView). ---`, each member with a one-line doc: `slotBar` (`"SlotBar"`), `slotChipChoiceList` (`"SlotChipChoiceList"`) and `recordExperimentButton` (`"RecordExperimentButton"`). (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each declaration with a one-line doc: `type Setups.SlotRole with member this.uiKey : ConstructorUiKey`, the role's `text` (step 257) without its spaces (`Source`, `Prep1`, `Obj2`, `Analyzer1`, `Detector1`); on the `ConstructorUiId` extension that holds `ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs:elementHover`, `static member slotChip (role : Setups.SlotRole) : ConstructorUiId` (`SlotChip_<role.uiKey>`) and `static member slotChipChoice (role : Setups.SlotRole) (item : Kit.ItemId) : ConstructorUiId` (`SlotChipChoice_<role.uiKey>_<the item's GUID>`); `type Kit.ItemLabel with member this.caption : ControlCaption`, the label's text; `type Angle with member this.degreeCaption : ControlCaption`, its degrees as the rotation bar writes them (`RotationControls.fs:51`, `BarDegrees.text`: at most two decimals, invariant culture) followed by `°`; and `type Setups.RoledSlot with member this.chipCaption (items : Kit.Item list) : ControlCaption`: `<role.text>: <the label of the item the slot holds>`, `<role.text>: —` when it holds nothing and `<role.text>: (not in this kit)` when `items` lacks its item, an `ObjectSlotRole` holding an item adding ` @ <slot.turnAngle.degreeCaption>` (step 277), the angle the naming template writes for it (step 271). (3) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/SlotBarView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.SlotBarView`, compiled directly before `TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj` and no comment, and a module doc of one to three lines. It declares, each with a one-line doc: `SlotChipState = { roled : Setups.RoledSlot; caption : ControlCaption; fitting : Kit.Item list }`, one chip; `SlotBarState = { chips : SlotChipState list; openOpt : Library.ElementId option; recordAvailability : ControlAvailability }`; and `SlotBarHandlers = { toggleChip : Library.ElementId -> unit; swapSlot : Library.ElementId -> Kit.ItemId -> unit; pickByLetter : Library.ElementId -> Setups.PickLetter -> unit; recordExperiment : unit -> unit }`; and `slotBarView (state : SlotBarState) (handlers : SlotBarHandlers) : IView`, documented in one to three lines. The view is a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `slotBar`, margin 8, 4, holding: (a) a `WrapPanel` (in a vertical block, AGENTS.md) of one chip per `chips` entry, in order, then, when `recordAvailability` is `ControlOffered`, the verb `Record experiment` (`MaterialsWindowView.verbButton`, public since step 107, carrying `recordExperimentButton`, calling `recordExperiment`). A chip is a `Border` carrying `slotChip roled.role`, focusable and a tab stop, in the box look of `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` (on `positiveBackground` while its list is open), whose child reads `<caption> ▾`; a press focuses it and calls `toggleChip` with its slot; a text typed while it has the focus is read by `PickLetter.tryCreate` (step 277), an answer calling `pickByLetter` with its slot, the event handled. So Tab moves between the chips in light order and a letter picks. (b) While `openOpt` names a chip's slot: a `WrapPanel` carrying `slotChipChoiceList` holding, for each item of that chip's `fitting`, a box carrying `slotChipChoice role item.id` with `item.label.caption`: the item the slot holds an `actionButton` on `positiveBackground` that calls `toggleChip` (closing the list: there is nothing to swap), every other a `verbButton` that calls `swapSlot` with the slot and the item; with no fitting item, the line `No item of this kit fits <role.text>.`. Every id is an AutomationId. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: on the model extension holding `slotChipItems` (step 279), `member model.slotBarState : SlotBarView.SlotBarState`: a chip per `SetupSlot.inLightOrder model.elements` (step 257), in that order, captioned by `chipCaption model.kitItems` and listing `model.slotChipItems slot`; `openOpt` is `slotChipOpenOpt`; and `recordAvailability` is `model.kitWrites` (step 185). A private `slotBarHandlers (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : SlotBarView.SlotBarHandlers` beside `experimentHandlers` dispatches `ToggleSlotChip`, `SwapSlot` and `RecordExperiment`, and resolves `pickByLetter` against the model: the slot of that id in `elements`, its `pickedByLetter letter (model.slotChipItems slot)` and `SwapSlot` of the picked item, no pick dispatching nothing. `mainView`'s table surface (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:3944`, `tableSurface`) becomes a `DockPanel` whose top is `SlotBarView.slotBarView model.slotBarState (slotBarHandlers model dispatch)` and whose fill is the panel it holds today, so the canvas, its gestures, the element menu overlay and the page's scrolling are unchanged; a full-surface bay shows no table and no bar. The comment above it gains, in no more words than it needs, that the slot bar sits above the table. No other message, field, id or option is added. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SlotBarTests.fs`, `module SlotBarTests` in `namespace OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, mounting `mainView` in a `HostWindow` as `ScrollExtentTests.fs:constructorWindow` (`:107`) mounts it, headless at 1000 × 900, over `initMain ()` driven through its messages: its scratch kit holds the items `Laser` (the HeNe preset), `LP1` and `LP2` (the linear-polarizer preset, `FixedMounting`), `QZ` and `QZ2` (the glass plates at version 1), added through the Items panel's messages (`OpenAddItemForm`, `ChooseNewItemModel`, `SetNewItemLabel`, `AddItem`, step 239), and a linear polarizer and a sample are added (`AddElement`) so that the light meets them in that order before the seeded detector. Without a trait: `the slot bar UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`: the three fixed ids' texts; `slotChip` of `SourceSlotRole`, `PrepSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)`, `ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 2)`, `AnalyzerSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)` and `DetectorSlotRole (SlotPosition 1)` is `SlotChip_Source`, `SlotChip_Prep1`, `SlotChip_Obj2`, `SlotChip_Analyzer1` and `SlotChip_Detector1`; and `slotChipChoice (ObjectSlotRole (SlotPosition 1))` of a test-local item id is `SlotChipChoice_Obj1_<its GUID>`. `the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle`: with `Laser`, `LP1` and `QZ` assigned to the source, the polarizer and the sample (`AssignSlot`, step 263) and the sample turned to R1 45° (`RotSetAxis (R1, BarDegrees 45.0)`, it being selected), the chips of Source, Prep 1, Obj 1 and Detector 1 are present left to right on one row, reading `Source: Laser ▾`, `Prep 1: LP1 ▾`, `Obj 1: QZ @ 45° ▾` and `Detector 1: — ▾`, and the bar's bottom is above the top of `tableElementCanvas`. `an open chip lists only the kit's items that fit its slot`: after `ToggleSlotChip` of the polarizer, `slotChipChoiceList` holds the boxes `slotChipChoice` of `LP1` and `LP2` and none of `Laser`, `QZ` or `QZ2`; after `ToggleSlotChip` of the detector it holds the line `No item of this kit fits Detector 1.`. `Tab moves between the chips in light order, and a typed letter picks the next fitting item`: over `the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle`'s model, with the Prep 1 chip focused, one Tab (`KeyPressQwerty` then `KeyReleaseQwerty` of `PhysicalKey.Tab`, as `EmbeddedChartTests.fs:156` presses Enter) leaves the Obj 1 chip focused (the window's `FocusManager`), and a second the Detector 1 chip; with the Obj 1 chip focused, `window.KeyTextInput("q")` (as `FacetedTreeControlsTests.fs:403` types) makes the sample hold `QZ2`; with it focused again, a second `q` makes it hold `QZ`, and `x` changes nothing. With trait `ui-smoke`, pressing boxes at their centre as `LibraryWindowTests.fs:clickOn` (`:69`) does: `pressing a chip and an item swaps the table to a kit setup that holds it`: over `the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle`'s model, pressing the Obj 1 chip shows `slotChipChoiceList`, and pressing `QZ2`'s box closes it, the chip reading `Obj 1: QZ2 @ 45° ▾` and the scratch kit's `readSetups ()` answering one setup whose sample slot holds `QZ2`. `pressing Record experiment twice records two experiments over the active setup`: with `SetSetupName (ControlCaption "Bench")`, `CreateSetup` and the polarizer chosen (`ExpChooseElement`), pressing `recordExperimentButton` twice leaves the scratch kit's `readExperiments ()` answering `E1` and `E2`, both over `'Bench' revision 1`. `KitWindowTests` (steps 185, 262): `a read-only window withholds every write control` also finds no `recordExperimentButton`.

**Acceptance.** After the slot bar lands, `SlotBarView.slotBarView` MUST show, directly above the table, one focusable chip per slot in light order under `ConstructorUiId.slotChip`, each naming its item and an object its angle, the open chip's list of fitting items under `slotChipChoice` sending `SwapSlot`, Tab moving between the chips and a typed letter picking, and `Record experiment` sending `RecordExperiment`, withheld under a read-only kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing a chip and an item swaps the table to a kit setup that holds it` and `pressing Record experiment twice records two experiments over the active setup`, the count rising by 2; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the slot bar UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the slot bar shows one chip per slot in light order above the table, each naming its item and an object its angle`, `an open chip lists only the kit's items that fit its slot` and `Tab moves between the chips in light order, and a typed letter picks the next fitting item` and the changed `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the sixteen s28 invariants MUST pass.
